# Kiosk dconf profile — selected per-account with DCONF_PROFILE=kiosk (see
# ../../skel/.config/environment.d/, planted by the lab kickstart), so it applies
# to opilas and to nobody else on the same machine.
#
# Order matters: dconf reads the databases below in DECREASING priority, so the
# `kiosk` db (defaults + locks, from db/kiosk.d/) wins over the fleet-wide
# `local` db (db/local.d/), and both are read-only under the user's writable db.
# The locks in db/kiosk.d/locks/ therefore bind this profile only — a staff
# account on the same machine, reading the default `user` profile, never sees
# them.
user-db:user
system-db:kiosk
system-db:local
